## Code Quality Standards to Always Enforce

### Laravel
- Controllers must be thin — no business logic, only: receive request → call service → return response
- Always use FormRequest classes for validation — never `$request->validate()` inside a controller
- Always use API Resources for data passed to Inertia — never raw models or `->toArray()`
- Always use named routes — never hardcoded URLs
- Always use route model binding — `{product:slug}` not `{id}`
- Always use Policies for authorization — never `if ($user->role === 'admin')` in controllers
- Always use `$fillable` on models — never `$guarded = []`
- Always use soft deletes on major models (Product, Category, Order, User)
- Always add database indexes on foreign keys and frequently queried columns
- Always wrap multiple DB operations in `DB::transaction()`
- Always use `.env` for sensitive config — never hardcode keys or secrets

### Vue / Inertia
- Always use `<script setup>` with Composition API — never Options API
- Always type props with `defineProps<{}>()` TypeScript generics
- Always use `useForm()` from `@inertiajs/vue3` for form submissions — never raw axios
- Always use `<Link>` from `@inertiajs/vue3` for internal links — never `<a href>`
- Always handle loading state on buttons during form submission (`form.processing`)
- Always display validation errors from `form.errors.fieldName`
- Always use named route helper `route('name')` via Ziggy — never hardcode URLs
- Never mutate props directly — use emits or local reactive copies
- Never use `any` type in TypeScript without a comment explaining why
- Always clean up event listeners and intervals in `onUnmounted()`

### Tailwind CSS
- Always use design system tokens from the project brief (colors, spacing, radius, shadows)
- Never write custom CSS unless Tailwind cannot achieve it
- Never use arbitrary values like `w-[347px]` unless truly necessary — prefer standard scale
- Always use responsive prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`) for layout shifts
- Never mix Tailwind with inline `style=""` attributes

